BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ev_draconids_1008-2026-10-08@coastaleventures.com
DTSTAMP:20261006T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261008
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261010
SUMMARY:Draconid Meteor Shower: the one that happens at bedtime
LOCATION:Your own yard\, or Big Lagoon State Park for a darker sky\, 12301 
 Gulf Beach Hwy\, Pensacola\, FL 32507
DESCRIPTION:Thu 10/08/2026 · from dark\, best in the first hours\n\nNearly
  every meteor shower asks you to be awake at three in the morning. The Dra
 conids do not: the radiant is highest as the sky goes dark\, so the best h
 our is the one right after dinner. The moon is a four percent crescent tha
 t does not rise until quarter to five\, which means the sky is as black as
  it gets all month.\n\nPrice: Free\n\nDetails: https://coastaleventures.co
 m/events/ev-draconids-1008.html
URL:https://coastaleventures.com/events/ev-draconids-1008.html
CATEGORIES:STEM and learning
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
